 119:     Rule
 120:     Use the largest sparse rectangular perimeter as the frame. Clear that frame
 121:     region and the external sprite pixels to background, draw a solid one-pixel
 122:     border in the frame color, solidify each sparse sprite into its contiguous
 123:     two-step mask, and place the sprites inside the frame with equal gaps.
 124:     Wide frames receive sprites left-to-right by source position; tall frames
 125:     receive them top-to-bottom by source position.
 126: 
 127:     Key insight
 128:     The frame supplies ordered slots: the sprite-to-slot assignment is by visible
 129:     source order, not by numeric color or by matching individual cells.
